== Effect ==
* If an activated item would regain its second to last charge upon clearing a room, it is instead fully charged. This effectively reduces its charge time by one bar.

== Notes ==
* Does not affect items with only one bar of charge or those with automatic recharge.
* Recharging an item by taking damage with {{i|Habit}}, the instant charge given by {{i|9 Volt}}, or any source of charge other than clearing a room, will not activate the trinket's effect.

== Synergies ==
* {{A|Golden Trinket}} / {{i|Mom's Box}}: Items require one charge unit fewer to get fully charged. {{dlc|r}} This effect stacks up to 3 fewer charges.
* {{i|9 Volt}}: If active item requires three or more charges, trinket gives an extra charge, effectively utilizing itself with 9 Volt.
* {{i|Jacob's Ladder}} / {{i|120 Volt}}: Increases the amount of arcs a spark can generate.
* {{i|Schoolbag}}: The trinket activates based on the primary item slot, but it grants an extra point of charge to the second item as well.
* {{i|The Battery|r}}: If an active item would have at least one level of charge upon clearing a room, an extra point of charge is granted by the trinket.

== Interactions ==
* {{i|4.5 Volt}}: AAA Battery has no effect after picking up 4.5 Volt.
* {{t|Watch Battery}}: Watch Battery triggering after clearing a room will also trigger AAA Battery, provided the activated item was missing exactly 3 charges prior to clearing the room.

